think Loaded KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then REMEMBER, REDS, session-logs top rows. Standfast clear: every living REDS row (80, 83, 84, 85, 81, 78, 86, 87) closed or released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a deep-debride custody gate, not agent-closable). No open agent-closable reds -- so this lap grows Season G open-media.
think The running thread is the Season G image family; live edge image/threshold.rye GREEN. Threshold's next-siblings named region MOMENTS/orientation as the second-moment companion of centroid (the lap two before). Lindy-first crux-first among the agent-doable siblings takes it: the hardest-solvable that opens the rest (orientation, tracking, shape descriptors) and the natural extension of the freshly-built centroid -- first moment to second moment.
think Ceilings: qoi_max_dim 8192, qoi_max_pixels 1<<20. The exact scaled-moment formula (area*mu20 = area*sum_xx - sum_x^2) overflows u64 at the extreme (area*sum_xx ~ 6.7e19 > 2^64). So accumulate the second CENTRAL moments about the rounded centroid in a bounded second pass: mu20/mu02 in u64 (<= area*dim^2 ~ 6.7e13), the signed cross moment mu11 in i64 (+/- 6.7e13). Honest cost named: deviations about the rounded center add at most a half-pixel of spread on a large blob; exact for a symmetric blob whose center lands on a pixel, so the witness uses exact-center fixtures.
think Compose not braid: moments asks image/centroid.rye for each component's center (the first moment it owns), then measures the spread around it -- the two readers stack rather than duplicate. label owns the LabelMap. Orientation = 0.5*atan2(2*mu11, mu20-mu02); eccentricity = sqrt(1 - lambda_min/lambda_max) over the eigenvalues of [[mu20,mu11],[mu11,mu02]]. Both are functions over the stored integers, no image written.
think Designed the decisive crux before coding: a diagonal and an anti-diagonal of the same five pixels share area (5), bounding box (5x5), and center (2,2) -- every fact regions and centroid measure agrees -- yet their cross moments are +10 and -10, so orientation splits +45 and -45. The lean no earlier reader can see.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no algorithm reds. atan2 two-arg form (std.math.atan2(y, x)) built clean. TAME caught four compound asserts (a and b) -- split each into two named halves, re-GREEN. width + ASCII + living-docs + living-card all clean.
obs Isotropy named honestly: a solid square has mu20==mu02, mu11==0, so the second moment cannot orient it -- orientation returns 0 by convention, eccentricity 0. The witness proves the diagonal line is provably more eccentric than the square, so eccentricity is a real ordered fact.
